⚠️ Error / Problem Faced

The catalog kept reloading forever and the browser's network tab filled with hundreds of /api/products calls.

The function that loaded the catalog was created again on every render, so React's useEffect saw a "new" function each time and ran again, in a loop.

After adding an item from the catalog sheet, the Bag tab still showed "empty" until the page was refreshed.

After installing a new package, Vite showed "504 Outdated Optimize Dep".

✅ Resolution
Kept the loaded catalog in a useRef and fetched it only when it was empty, so it loads once.
Re-read the bag from the server whenever the user switches tabs, so the screen always matches the server.
Restarted the Vite dev server after installing new packages.

🖼️ Project Picture

Customer home screen showing the scan card, the bag summary and the five showrooms of the mall.

💡 Learning

We learned how React's useEffect dependencies work and how a changing function can cause an infinite loop.

We also learned that the server is the source of truth, and the screen should re-read it instead of guessing.

